%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 7c7c947f0ccabb24dbf991df8e9f6d4f, type: 3}
  m_Name: in-service TE
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  defaultQuestions:
  - QuestionText: What is the primary target group for in-service teacher education?
    Options:
    - Aspiring teachers before they start their career
    - Working teachers already in the profession
    - School principals and administrators only
    - Parents and community members
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: in-service TE
  - QuestionText: 'The concept of in-service teacher education is best described
      as a:'
    Options:
    - One-time induction program
    - Voluntary activity with no clear goals
    - Replacement for pre-service education
    - Continuous and lifelong process
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: in-service TE
  - QuestionText: Which of the following is a key reason for the need for in-service
      teacher education?
    Options:
    - To eliminate the need for pre-service training
    - To keep teachers updated with rapid changes in knowledge and pedagogy
    - To reduce the number of working days for teachers
    - To standardize teacher salaries
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: in-service TE
  - QuestionText: 'The main purpose of in-service teacher education is to:'
    Options:
    - Criticize teachers for their shortcomings
    - Replace experienced teachers with new ones
    - Provide teachers with a vacation from their routine
    - Improve the quality of classroom instruction and student learning
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: in-service TE
  - QuestionText: Which of the following falls within the scope of in-service teacher
      education?
    Options:
    - Awarding initial teaching degrees
    - Training in the use of new educational technology
    - Recruiting new teachers
    - Designing school buildings
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: in-service TE
  - QuestionText: 'The term "INSET" is an acronym for:'
    Options:
    - International Service for Education and Training
    - Integrated System for Educational Technology
    - Initial Service and Educational Theory
    - In-Service Teacher Education
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: in-service TE
  - QuestionText: 'A workshop on implementing the National Education Policy (NEP)
      2020 in classrooms is an example of:'
    Options:
    - Pre-service education
    - In-service education
    - Student counseling
    - Parent-teacher association work
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: in-service TE
  - QuestionText: Which factor has LEAST contributed to the growing need for in-service
      teacher education?
    Options:
    - Static and unchanging nature of knowledge
    - Development of new pedagogical theories
    - Increasing diversity in student populations
    - Advancements in information technology
    CorrectOptionIndex: 0
    LevelName: in-service TE
  - QuestionText: 'The purpose of in-service education that focuses on training teachers
      to handle children with special needs is to promote:'
    Options:
    - Competitive learning
    - Inclusive education
    - Streamlining the curriculum
    - Standardized testing
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: in-service TE
  - QuestionText: Which of the following is a key characteristic of effective in-service
      teacher education?
    Options:
    - It is disconnected from teachers' classroom realities.
    - It is a one-way lecture from an expert.
    - It is relevant and directly applicable to teachers' work.
    - It is mandatory and punitive in nature.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: in-service TE
  - QuestionText: 'A teacher attending a course on "Flipped Classroom Models" is
      engaging in in-service education to:'
    Options:
    - Fulfill a mandatory requirement for promotion
    - Update their pedagogical skills with a new teaching strategy
    - Replace their basic teaching qualification
    - Avoid classroom teaching for a few days
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: in-service TE
  - QuestionText: The scope of in-service education includes training in which of
      the following?
    Options:
    - Only subject content knowledge
    - Only co-curricular activities
    - Only administrative duties
    - All aspects of a teacher's professional role, including pedagogy, assessment,
      and counseling
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: in-service TE
  - QuestionText: 'The philosophy underlying in-service teacher education is that
      teacher learning should be:'
    Options:
    - Confined to the pre-service phase
    - A lifelong endeavor
    - The sole responsibility of the teacher
    - Focused only on theoretical knowledge
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: in-service TE
  - QuestionText: Which of the following is a major challenge in implementing effective
      in-service teacher education programs in India?
    Options:
    - Lack of any need for teacher development
    - Absence of a national curriculum framework
    - Over-qualification of all teachers
    - Inadequate funding and logistical support
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: in-service TE
  - QuestionText: 'The "NISHTHA" program launched by the Government of India is a
      prime example of a:'
    Options:
    - Pre-service teacher training program
    - Large-scale in-service teacher training initiative
    - Student scholarship scheme
    - School infrastructure development plan
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: in-service TE
  - QuestionText: 'A key difference between pre-service and in-service teacher education
      is that in-service education is:'
    Options:
    - More theoretical
    - Focused on initial qualification
    - Job-embedded and continuous
    - Only for elementary teachers
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: in-service TE
  - QuestionText: 'The purpose of conducting in-service programs on "Continuous and
      Comprehensive Evaluation (CCE)" is to:'
    Options:
    - Promote rote learning and memorization
    - Train teachers in diverse and continuous assessment methods
    - Eliminate all forms of student assessment
    - Focus only on year-end examinations
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: in-service TE
  - QuestionText: Which of the following is within the scope of in-service education
      for professional development?
    Options:
    - Learning action research methodologies
    - Taking attendance
    - Supervising school meals
    - Managing school finances
    CorrectOptionIndex: 0
    LevelName: in-service TE
  - QuestionText: 'The need for in-service education arises partly from the fact
      that pre-service education:'
    Options:
    - Is always perfect and requires no follow-up
    - Cannot prepare teachers for all the challenges of a dynamic classroom
    - Is not a recognized form of education
    - Is more important than experience
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: in-service TE
  - QuestionText: 'A seminar on "Integrating Mental Health Awareness in Teaching"
      serves the purpose of:'
    Options:
    - Increasing teacher workload unnecessarily
    - Enhancing the teacher's ability to support holistic student development
    - Replacing the school counselor's role
    - Focusing only on academic outcomes
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: in-service TE
  - QuestionText: 'The scope of in-service education extends to helping teachers
      understand and address:'
    Options:
    - Only the academic needs of high-achieving students
    - Administrative paperwork
    - Only the syllabus prescribed in the textbook
    - The learning needs of a diverse student population, including marginalized
      groups
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: in-service TE
  - QuestionText: 'A teacher participating in an online certification course on "Blended
      Learning" during their service is engaging in:'
    Options:
    - A pre-service qualification
    - A form of in-service professional development
    - An unrelated hobby
    - A mandatory government test
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: in-service TE
  - QuestionText: 'The fundamental concept of in-service teacher education aligns
      with the principle of:'
    Options:
    - Fixed ability
    - Lifelong learning
    - Static knowledge
    - One-time training
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: in-service TE
  - QuestionText: Which of the following is a primary need for in-service education
      in the 21st century?
    Options:
    - To reduce the use of technology in classrooms
    - To isolate teachers from global educational trends
    - To encourage traditional chalk-and-talk methods only
    - To prepare teachers for the integration of ICT in education
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: in-service TE
  - QuestionText: 'The "District Institute of Education and Training (DIET)" in India
      plays a significant role in:'
    Options:
    - Pre-service teacher education only
    - Providing in-service training to elementary school teachers
    - Higher education research
    - International student exchange
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: in-service TE
  - QuestionText: 'A key purpose of in-service education is to foster a teacher''s
      identity as a:'
    Options:
    - Passive implementer of directives
    - Reflective practitioner and change agent
    - Isolated worker
    - Bureaucratic official
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: in-service TE
  - QuestionText: 'The scope of in-service education regarding curriculum includes:'
    Options:
    - Blindly implementing the curriculum without question
    - Creating a personal curriculum unrelated to national goals
    - Ignoring national curriculum frameworks
    - Understanding, interpreting, and effectively transacting the curriculum
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: in-service TE
  - QuestionText: 'A teacher who attends a program to learn how to use a new software
      for creating interactive quizzes is addressing the need to:'
    Options:
    - Increase paperwork
    - Improve technological pedagogical skills
    - Replace human teachers with software
    - Avoid direct interaction with students
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: in-service TE
  - QuestionText: 'The concept of "continuous professional development" (CPD) is
      synonymous with the modern view of:'
    Options:
    - Pre-service teacher education
    - School administration
    - Student assessment
    - In-service teacher education
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: in-service TE
  - QuestionText: 'A major purpose of in-service education is to orient teachers
      to:'
    Options:
    - Their personal financial investments
    - New educational policies and national missions
    - The political affiliations of students
    - The architectural design of schools
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: in-service TE
  - QuestionText: 'The scope of in-service education for a science teacher could
      include a workshop on:'
    Options:
    - New discoveries and experiments in their field
    - The history of art
    - Advanced literary criticism
    - Musical notation
    CorrectOptionIndex: 0
    LevelName: in-service TE
  - QuestionText: 'The need for in-service education is most critically driven by
      the goal of:'
    Options:
    - Maintaining the status quo in education
    - Improving educational quality and student achievement
    - Reducing the number of teachers
    - Standardizing teacher attire
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: in-service TE
  - QuestionText: 'A program designed to train teachers in conflict resolution and
      peer mediation techniques falls under the scope of:'
    Options:
    - Student discipline only
    - Enhancing teachers' professional competencies in classroom management and social
      skills
    - Legal training for teachers
    - Extracurricular activity management
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: in-service TE
  - QuestionText: 'The fundamental concept of in-service teacher education rejects
      the idea that:'
    Options:
    - Learning is lifelong
    - Teacher training ends with pre-service education
    - Collaboration is useful
    - Practice can be improved
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: in-service TE
  - QuestionText: Which of the following is a key indicator of a successful in-service
      teacher education program?
    Options:
    - Teachers feel entertained.
    - The program lasted for a very long time.
    - The program was delivered by a famous speaker.
    - Teachers can directly apply what they learned to improve their classroom practice.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: in-service TE
  - QuestionText: 'The purpose of in-service education that focuses on "action research"
      is to enable teachers to:'
    Options:
    - Become theoretical researchers in universities
    - Systematically study and solve problems in their own classrooms
    - Avoid teaching responsibilities
    - Criticize educational policies
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: in-service TE
  - QuestionText: 'The scope of in-service education is influenced by:'
    Options:
    - Only the teacher's personal interests
    - The uniform design of the school
    - The weather conditions of the region
    - The changing needs of the society, students, and the education system
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: in-service TE
  - QuestionText: 'A teacher participating in a peer observation and feedback program
      is engaging in a form of:'
    Options:
    - Summative evaluation for promotion
    - Collaborative in-service professional development
    - Pre-service training
    - Disciplinary action
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: in-service TE
  - QuestionText: 'The need for in-service education becomes more critical in an
      era of:'
    Options:
    - Educational stagnation
    - Globalization and rapid change
    - Fixed and unchanging job roles
    - De-professionalization of teaching
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: in-service TE
  - QuestionText: 'A core purpose of in-service education is to combat:'
    Options:
    - Teacher enthusiasm
    - Parental involvement
    - Student attendance
    - Professional obsolescence
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: in-service TE
  - QuestionText: 'Training on "Differentiated Instruction" falls within the scope
      of in-service education aimed at:'
    Options:
    - Teaching all students in the same way
    - Catering to individual learning differences in a mixed-ability classroom
    - Streamlining the assessment process
    - Reducing teacher planning time
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: in-service TE
  - QuestionText: The concept of in-service teacher education is best supported by
      which ancient Indian saying?
    Options:
    - '"Vasudhaiva Kutumbakam"'
    - '"Satyameva Jayate"'
    - '"Aa no bhadraha kratavo yantu vishwataha" (Let noble thoughts come from all
      directions)'
    - '"Sarvam Khalvidam Brahma"'
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: in-service TE
  - QuestionText: 'A key need for in-service education identified by the NEP 2020
      is to:'
    Options:
    - Reduce the number of teachers
    - Prepare teachers for a 5+3+3+4 curricular structure
    - Eliminate all teacher training
    - Focus only on STEM education
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: in-service TE
  - QuestionText: 'The purpose of a "refresher course" in in-service education is
      to:'
    Options:
    - Refresh teachers by giving them a break
    - Update and renew knowledge in a specific subject area
    - Replace old teachers with new ones
    - Criticize outdated teaching methods
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: in-service TE
  - QuestionText: 'The scope of in-service education for school leadership includes
      training for the role of:'
    Options:
    - Only a classroom teacher
    - Only a parent
    - Only a student
    - A mentor teacher or head of department
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: in-service TE
  - QuestionText: 'The concept of in-service education implies that professional
      competence is:'
    Options:
    - Static and fixed at the start of a career
    - Dynamic and needs continuous nurturing
    - Irrelevant to student learning
    - Solely dependent on personal talent
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: in-service TE
  - QuestionText: 'A workshop on "Creating a Positive Learning Environment" addresses
      the need to:'
    Options:
    - Focus only on academic content
    - Improve the psychological and emotional climate of the classroom
    - Decorate the classroom walls
    - Strictly control student behavior
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: in-service TE
  - QuestionText: 'The ultimate purpose of all in-service teacher education is to
      enhance:'
    Options:
    - Teacher salaries
    - The complexity of the curriculum
    - The reputation of the school
    - Student learning experiences and outcomes
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: in-service TE
  - QuestionText: 'The scope of in-service education, therefore, is not limited to
      a few topics but is:'
    Options:
    - Narrow and specialized
    - Holistic and all-encompassing of a teacher's professional life
    - Focused only on one pedagogical method
    - Concerned only with subject content
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: in-service TE
